  Sketching uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  All three use the same four groups, made from your current 12 fields:
  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  The layouts:
  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m a headed section per group, all in one scrolling column. This is the smallest change.
  - [1mB. Sidebar:[0m the same sections, plus a left-hand menu that jumps to each group.
  - [1mC. Tabs:[0m only one group shows at a time. This needs some JavaScript, and care so fields on hidden tabs still get
    saved.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. Twelve fields is too few to justify a menu or tabs, A needs no JavaScript, and the save behavior stays
  exactly the same. Any of the three keeps the existing form submission working.

